    {
      "id": "45ad163102f81f7bf84c5eec6d7a8a8ad59843bb",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 2094738747,
          "type": null,
          "body": "> Because that's how Vector Informatik's software writes them with a bad date/time, or because they were damaged by a third party?\n\nI don't know what happened to this particular file I have, but it looks like it's truncated at the end (the file ends in the middle of the last log container). Maybe the writing has been interrupted before it finished. In any case, Wireshark can read it fine, up until the penultimate log container, but the header is all zeroes (except for the essential data like the magic and header size), probably because Vector's software writes all the info at the end. I tried opening the file in CANoe and it doesn't complain at all.\n\nIn the end I think it's fine to assume a timestamp of 0 in case there's any recoverable corruption.",
          "author": {
            "id": 18219493,
            "username": "giovanni.musto",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Giovanni Musto",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/b8ca1135be5e614246a54ed49c6809a9b172aafdcb27c2db7ec5548b625e76d5?s=80&d=identicon",
